WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.990
Lucía writes about her
brother's weekend: Fue a Madrid.

2
00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:07.230
Then about her exam: Fue difícil.

3
00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:09.650
The same little word, twice.

4
00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:12.570
But look it up, and you'll find
it listed under two different

5
00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:13.590
verbs.

6
00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:16.550
So which verb is
Lucía using each time,

7
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:18.870
and how is anyone supposed to tell?

8
00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:22.290
In this mission, you'll meet
three everyday verbs that break

9
00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:23.750
the regular pattern.

10
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:28.160
Then you'll learn a big group
with brand-new stems: tuve,

11
00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:29.530
estuve, pude.

12
00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:32.770
You'll spot their giveaway
endings with no accents,

13
00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:36.630
and lock in two tricky
spellings: hizo, dijeron.

14
00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:42.250
Your mission: work out which
verb is hiding behind each fue.
